                "tags": [
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2019-1010022",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2019-1010022"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2019-1010022?s=debian&n=glibc&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "GNU Libc current is affected by: Mitigation bypass. The impact is: Attacker may bypass stack guard protection. The component is: nptl. The attack vector is: Exploit stack buffer overflow vulnerability and use this bypass vulnerability to bypass stack guard. NOTE: Upstream comments indicate \"this is being treated as a non-security bug and no real threat.\n\n---\n- glibc <unfixed> (unimportant)\nNot treated as a security issue by upstream\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=22850\n",
                "markdown": "> GNU Libc current is affected by: Mitigation bypass. The impact is: Attacker may bypass stack guard protection. The component is: nptl. The attack vector is: Exploit stack buffer overflow vulnerability and use this bypass vulnerability to bypass stack guard. NOTE: Upstream comments indicate \"this is being treated as a non-security bug and no real threat.\n\n---\n- glibc <unfixed> (unimportant)\nNot treated as a security issue by upstream\nhttps://sourceware.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=22850\n\n|                                                                                                      |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/glibc@2.41-12%2Bdeb13u4?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                                    |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                             |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
