            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-75806",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-75806"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-75806?s=debian&n=openssl&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3C3.5.7-1%7Edeb13u3",
              "help": {
                "text": "Issue summary: An established DTLS 1.2 association using an AEAD cipher suite can be terminated by a single unauthenticated datagram whose encrypted fragment is shorter than the mandatory explicit IV and authentication tag overhead.  Impact summary: An attacker who can send a datagram that is routed to an existing DTLS 1.2 association can tear that association down without knowing any key material. This is a Denial of Service limited to the targeted association. There is no memory safety or confidentiality impact.  CWE: CWE-1284: Improper Validation of Specified Quantity in Input  Description: In TLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.2 every record protected by an AEAD cipher suite carries an explicit IV followed by the ciphertext and an authentication tag. When decrypting such a record the record layer passed the record length to the cipher implementation before checking that the record was long enough to contain the explicit IV and the tag. For a record shorter than that overhead the cipher implementation rejected the impossible length, and the record layer treated this as an internal failure and raised a fatal internal_error alert instead of treating the record as one that failed authentication.  In TLS 1.2 the same record causes a fatal internal_error alert instead of the expected bad_record_mac alert. Since any undecryptable record already terminates a TLS connection, this is a protocol conformance issue rather than a security issue in TLS.  The fix validates the record length against the explicit IV and tag length before any AEAD processing, so that TLS reports bad_record_mac and DTLS silently discards the record.  FIPS impact: no The affected code is outside the FIPS module boundary.\n\n---\n- openssl 3.6.5-1\nhttps://openssl-library.org/news/secadv/20260929.txt\n",
                "markdown": "> Issue summary: An established DTLS 1.2 association using an AEAD cipher suite can be terminated by a single unauthenticated datagram whose encrypted fragment is shorter than the mandatory explicit IV and authentication tag overhead.  Impact summary: An attacker who can send a datagram that is routed to an existing DTLS 1.2 association can tear that association down without knowing any key material. This is a Denial of Service limited to the targeted association. There is no memory safety or confidentiality impact.  CWE: CWE-1284: Improper Validation of Specified Quantity in Input  Description: In TLS 1.2 and DTLS 1.2 every record protected by an AEAD cipher suite carries an explicit IV followed by the ciphertext and an authentication tag. When decrypting such a record the record layer passed the record length to the cipher implementation before checking that the record was long enough to contain the explicit IV and the tag. For a record shorter than that overhead the cipher implementation rejected the impossible length, and the record layer treated this as an internal failure and raised a fatal internal_error alert instead of treating the record as one that failed authentication.  In TLS 1.2 the same record causes a fatal internal_error alert instead of the expected bad_record_mac alert. Since any undecryptable record already terminates a TLS connection, this is a protocol conformance issue rather than a security issue in TLS.  The fix validates the record length against the explicit IV and tag length before any AEAD processing, so that TLS reports bad_record_mac and DTLS silently discards the record.  FIPS impact: no The affected code is outside the FIPS module boundary.\n\n---\n- openssl 3.6.5-1\nhttps://openssl-library.org/news/secadv/20260929.txt\n\n|                                                                                                      |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/openssl@3.5.7-1~deb13u2?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  <3.5.7-1~deb13u3                                                                      |\n|Fixed version   3.5.7-1~deb13u3                                                                       |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": "<3.5.7-1~deb13u3",
                "cvssV3_severity": "MEDIUM",
                "fixed_version": "3.5.7-1~deb13u3",
                "purls": [
