              "id": "CVE-2026-95619",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-95619"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-95619?s=debian&n=gcc-14&ns=debian&t=deb&osn=debian&osv=13&vr=%3E0",
              "help": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in libstdc++. An integer overflow can occur when processing large inputs to the aligned operator new in the C++ library. This vulnerability could lead to an undersized memory allocation, potentially causing memory corruption or application instability.\n\n---\n- gcc-15 <unfixed>\n- gcc-16 <unfixed>\n- gcc-14 <unfixed>\n- gcc-12 <unfixed>\nhttps://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/commit/59d235ffa5a69231eb42e5290d52dc8c90d28b7a\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2537811\n",
                "markdown": "> A flaw was found in libstdc++. An integer overflow can occur when processing large inputs to the aligned operator new in the C++ library. This vulnerability could lead to an undersized memory allocation, potentially causing memory corruption or application instability.\n\n---\n- gcc-15 <unfixed>\n- gcc-16 <unfixed>\n- gcc-14 <unfixed>\n- gcc-12 <unfixed>\nhttps://github.com/gcc-mirror/gcc/commit/59d235ffa5a69231eb42e5290d52dc8c90d28b7a\nhttps://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=2537811\n\n|                                                                                               |\n|Package         pkg:deb/debian/gcc-14@14.2.0-19?os_distro=trixie&os_name=debian&os_version=13  |\n|Affected range  >0                                                                             |\n|Fixed version   not fixed                                                                      |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
